A column's type changed with its data: kronor as integers become a price
written out as text, in a new column filled @from the old one, the old one
dropped.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 95), (2, 40);

== after
-- @release 1
-- @drop 1 column dish price_kr
-- @from 1 column dish price = CAST(price_kr AS TEXT) || ' kr'
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, price = CAST(price_kr AS TEXT) || ' kr'
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "price") SELECT "id", (
    CAST(price_kr AS TEXT) || ' kr'
    ) FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"
migrated from release 0

== query
SELECT id, price FROM dish ORDER BY id

== rows
1 | 95 kr
2 | 40 kr
